--- body ---
## Context

Child of 0029 (tracker). Ruling 7 of 2026-09-06 and its refinement of the same
day fix what a question and a score are: an answer is a paragraph in a page in
a file attached to a Zotero entry; a reply scores win, near-win or miss on the
rank of the answer paragraph and the completeness of its citation chain; the
same work in another rendering or language is a near-win; a no-answer question
carries an empty pinned set and is expected-miss. The pinned set is a set of
rows (a work, or a section of a work); two paragraphs in one section are one
row with alternates; `set_kind: any-of | all-of` says whether one row suffices
or all are needed (all-of keeps R34's absolute reading and the ladder reads on
the weakest row; per-row detail is reported). Rank and mean reciprocal rank are
reported per lane and never gated (D11).

## Question record (bank schema `menagerie-bank/v2`)
id; need (prose, written before any document was opened for need-driven
questions); query; question_language; answer_language (of the answer
paragraph); lane = the pair; signal (exact | paraphrase | agreement); mode
(lexical | semantic | hybrid | any); facet (core | notes | group | deep-body);
stratum (core | reserve); mechanisms; generator (need | hazard); set_kind;
pinned: list of rows, each `{work_id, recipe_id, attachment_id, section,
alternates: [{page_printed, char_offset, quote}], chain: {title, author, date,
identifier, section_heading, page_printed, part_title, part_byline}}`;
expected_miss (bool) and expected_miss_mechanism; reachability (computed:
per alternate, reachable in the export, offset resolved, stamped with the
extraction configuration); provenance {author, date, page_read}.

## Relevant files
- `bench/golden_gate.py` (scorer), `tests/test_golden_gate.py`
- `bench/fixtures/questions/` (the bank), `bench/fixtures/export/`
- `bench/fixtures/make_index_fixture.mjs` (replay), `bench/query.py`
- `Makefile` (`golden` target), `SPEC.md` §5.2.8

## Actions
1. Scorer v2: read the bank and a replies file (schema v2, v1 refused); per
   question win / near-win / miss, rank, chain completeness (fraction of the
   chain fields the reply carries correctly), expected-miss handling; readings
   per lane, per stratum, per format, per signal, per set_kind, with counts
   beside every rate and not-measured at zero; R34 absolute over the pinned
   rows and the stability reading as SPEC §5.2.8 states them.
2. Bank validator and reachability: locate every quoted alternate in the
   committed export, resolve char offsets, stamp the extraction configuration.
3. Runner: drive the bank's queries against the replay index of a zoteus
   build and emit a replies file in the v2 shape.
4. `make golden`: validator + scorer on the committed export and bank.
5. Author the bank: need-driven questions first, then hazard-driven, one per
   mechanism and tally sub-case; at least five per document with body text.

## Verification
- [ ] the scorer refuses a v1 bundle and a v2 bundle with a malformed row
- [ ] every rate prints its count; a lane with no question prints not-measured
- [ ] the bank validates against the committed export

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `bench/fixtures/questions/` committed, documented in
      `bench/fixtures/README.md`
- [ ] `bench/golden_gate.py` at input schema v2, `make golden` present
- [ ] the scorer's reading on the reviewed zoteus build recorded
